The Need for Performance Optimization
When handling large-scale web-scraping projects, slow performance can result in missed data or even HTTP bans. Therefore,
improving performance becomes essential, especially during data extraction from complex sites. This guide will delve into
advanced techniques involving parallelizing requests, optimizing HTML parsing, and reducing memory usage.

Parallelizing Requests with Multiprocessing 
Multiprocessing allows Python to create multiple processes, effectively enabling parallel  requests. This can significantly 
enhance the scraping speed when visiting numerous URLs. Using multiprocessing, you can distribute the workload across
different CPU cores, minimizing wait times and maximizing throughput.

